==Latin==
[[File:Uncrossed gladius.jpg|thumb|gladius (sword)]]

===Etymology===
Of {{etyl|cel|la}} origin, probably from {{etyl|cel-gau|la}} {{recons|kladyos||sword|lang=cel-gau}}, from {{etyl|cel-pro|la}} {{recons|kladiwos||sword|lang=cel-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|la}} {{recons|kola-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|klā-||to beat, break, kill|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with {{etyl|sga|-}} {{term|claideb||sword|lang=sga}}, {{etyl|cy|-}} {{term|cleddyf||sword|lang=cy}}, {{etyl|br|-}} {{term|klezeñv||sword|lang=br}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ˈɡla.di.us/|lang=la}}
* {{audio|la-cls-gladius.ogg|Audio (Classical)}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|gladius|gladii|gladiī|m|second}}

# [[sword]]
#: ''Mitte '''gladium''' in vaginam.''
#:: Put the '''sword''' into its sheath.
#: ''In '''gladium''' incumbere.''
#:: To fall on one's '''sword'''.
# {{figuratively|lang=la}} [[murder]], [[death]]
# a [[gladiatorial]] [[contest]]
# [[swordfish]]

